1 NOTE {geni:about_me} b4c3d11f5d12  '''Helena Barendina Roberta (Norbertha)''' * Bruinjjeshoogte, dist. Somerset East 12/20 11 1811 = Paarl 29 4 1812 + Middelburg Kp 27 11 1835 x Anglcan Church, Grahamstown 7 6 1827 Frans Johannes de Kl
2 CONC erk * 4 2 1809 = Graaff-Reinet 26 12 1809 son of. Barend Jacobus de Klerk and Johanna Maria du Rand (he xx Soimerset East 6 3 1836 Susanna Catharina Magdalena Mulder
2 CONT
2 CONT SAF Volume 3 page 449
2 CONT
2 CONT MOOC 7/1/210 Ref 16
2 CONT
2 CONT Will signed on 26 August 1836, of Frans Johannes de Klerk and Susanna Catharina Magdalena Mulder, both born in this country, living at Bruintjies Hoogden on the farm Doorn Kraal in Somerset district
2 CONT
2 CONT The portions of the testator's children from his first marriage to the late '''Helena Barendina Norberta Bester''', viz. Hilletjie Levina Catharina de Klerk, Barend Jacobus de Klerk and Johanna Maria Barendina Jacoba de Klerk, are
2 CONC  to be safeguarded by two honest and upright men.
2 CONT
2 CONT The surviving spouse is to be the sole and universal heir, and to ensure that the children receive a Christian education.
2 CONT
2 CONT If no children are born of the marriage, the testator's mother, Johanna Maria Durand, widow of the late Barend Jacobus de Klerk, is to receive her legitimate portion .
2 CONT If the surviving spouse remarries, the estate should be valued by two honest and upright men, to protect the portions due to the children.
